    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d94-a1-a13">

                <pb facs="0272" n="214" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg214"/>


                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Office Colonization,</hi> 13 <hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">San Juan de Letran</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-03-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 14, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your letter of January 30 has just been
                    received. You may rely upon the enclosed circular as accurate.</p>
                <p>The inducements offered to immigrants by imperial decree are exemption from
                    taxation, military conscription for a term of years, from the payment of all or
                    any import dues on personal effects or farming utensils, religious liberty, and
                    a grant of land of 640 acres to married men, or 320 to single, either gratis or
                    at low rates and accommodating terms.</p>
                <p>Very truly,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RICHARD L. MAURY, <hi rendition="#italic">Sub-Commissioner, late Colonel
                            C. S. Army.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reuben Herndon</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Galveston,Texas.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
